<http://www.mimo-db.eu/InstrumentsKeywords/8383> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> """A seasonal, polish folk instrument, made in the spring; would become porous and unplayable when it dried out; formerly a signal instrument (used by shepherds), often played by
			children, nowadays sometimes made as a music toy; body made from a spirally rolled piece of willow bark, fastened with a thorn ('przetyczka'); it should have a double reed ('bekas'), also
			made of willow bark, in the inlet""" .

